  "raw": {
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Lecturer-of-Human-Health-Sciences_R0153429": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Human Health Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for a Lecturer of Human Health Sciences with a background in anatomy and physiology, microbiology, and/or introductory biology. This is a 12-month position with opportunities to pursue promotion through the lecturer career ladder. The primary location for this position is the Henderson campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. The selected candidate will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team in the Department of Physical and Life Sciences, which supports Bachelor of Science degrees in Biology, Chemistry, Environmental Science, and Human Health Sciences. We hope to find a colleague with interest and potential to participate in interdisciplinary opportunities in curriculum development. As a Lecturer in the Human Health Sciences program, you will play a key role in integrating high-quality instruction and a supportive student learning experience in the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business. About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business and Department of Physical and Life Sciences at Nevada State: With committed faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ student-centered ethos cultivates civically engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the southern Nevada region and beyond. As the largest of three Schools at Nevada State University, our programs range across six departments – Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and Psychology and Counseling. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach 30 credits per academic year, which typically includes 12 credits in fall, 12 credits in spring, and 6 credits in the summer. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. Teach primarily lower-level courses in Anatomy and Physiology, Fundamentals of Life Science, and General Microbiology in an in-person format. Serve on departmental and university-wide committees. Engage in professional development activities. Required Qualifications: M.S. or terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D.) in one of the following fields or a related field: Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, or Microbiology. Candidates who are ABD will be considered with the   expectation that   the degree will be completed by June 30, 2027. Evidence of a strong commitment to teaching, educational excellence, and mentoring undergraduate students. Demonstrated commitment to a diverse, non-traditional, first-generation student population. Effective interpersonal, communication, and technology skills. Offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of due diligence background check and verification of credentials. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of instructional effectiveness at the college/university level. Evidence of teaching courses for pre-nursing students. Commitment to active/experiential learning. Experience or interest in developing curriculum at the university level. Rank, Salary & Benefits: 12-month. Non Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $62,503.00 . Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, 24 annual leave days, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, September 28, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by September 27 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted). The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process. Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice_R0153427": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice. The Department of History, Law, and Society is seeking two tenure-track positions in Criminal Justice. This position will teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. The primary location for this position is the Henderson campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. About Criminal Justice at Nevada State: Criminal Justice serves a student population of approximately 300 majors and minors. The program provides students with a foundation of criminal justice courses while incorporating social justice issues. We are seeking expertise and/or teaching experience in one or more of the following areas: legal issues, policing and corrections. Please be familiar with our course offerings and indicate which courses or areas you have experience teaching or are willing to teach. Course offerings are available here . About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. Teach lower- and upper-level courses in Criminal Justice in a variety of formats (e.g., in-person, hybrid, online). Please familiarize yourself with our course offerings. Serve on departmental and university-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning. Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Criminal Justice or Criminology. Candidates who are ABD will be considered with the   expectation that   the degree will be completed by June 30, 2027. Evidence of strong commitment to teaching, mentoring, and working with undergraduates. Demonstrated commitment to, or interest in, working with a diverse, non-traditional, first-generation student population. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity and/or experience with Canvas learning management system. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: criminal law, law and society, comparative criminal justice systems, immigration law, social inequality, policing, and/or corrections. Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $66,879.00. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Thursday, October 1, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by September 30 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted). The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process. Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Network---Systems-Administrator_R0153415": {
      "title": "Network & Systems Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Network & Systems Administrator. This position will be responsible for the implementation, administration, troubleshooting, monitoring, support, and documentation of Nevada State University network and server infrastructure. Essential job functions include monitoring and ensuring operational continuity of mission critical network, telecommunication, virtualization, server, and storage systems; researching, installing, configuring, and maintaining related hardware; providing and managing backup and disaster recovery; providing and managing related security; and working with other Information & Technology Services units to develop end-to-end solutions. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Implement, configure, manage, maintain, troubleshoot, secure, and monitor campus network and telecommunication systems. Implement, configure, manage, maintain, troubleshoot, secure, and monitor campus virtualization, server and storage infrastructure and systems. Manage network and datacenter security including configuring, supporting, testing, and monitoring campus firewalls, access control lists, intrusion detection/protection systems, directory services, etc. Develop, manage, maintain, test, and monitor disaster recovery and data backup/restoration services for mission critical systems. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in information systems, computer science, or related field or ten (10) years of professional experience demonstrating equivalent knowledge. Five (5) years of experience in network administration, system administration, and information security. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience administering network/server infrastructure in large, complex multi-user environments (primarily on Cisco/Meraki Systems, Windows Environments, Microsoft Server 2016, 2019, 2022, Windows 10/11, Active Directory, DNS, DHCP, Radius, GPO, Azure AD and Intune, KACE Appliances, Mix of Server Hardware, Dell/Lenovo). Experience with server virtualization (Nutanix, VMWare and Hyper-V). Experience with scripting and system automation (Windows Environments, Server 2016, 2019, 2022 and Windows 10/11). Salary & Benefits Budgeted salary for this position is $77,728.00. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, 24 annual leave days, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Wednesday, September 30, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply before September 29 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Speech-Language-Pathology_R0153368": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Speech-Language Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Speech-Language Pathology to start either Spring 2027 or Fall 2027, negotiated upon offer . The Assistant/Associate Professor will contribute to program development and academic leadership. Qualified candidates may be considered for department chair responsibilities in the future. Our campus is designated a Hispanic-Serving and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution, and we are looking for candidates with a demonstrated commitment to and success working in diverse, multicultural, and multilingual communities. Our program seeks candidates who are passionate about fostering success among our highly diverse student population as well as preparing students to advocate in a similar manner for their own clients/patients. Candidates should be able to teach speech-language pathology courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, particularly courses with a focus on adult neurological conditions. About School of Education at Nevada State: The School of Education (SOE) is an exciting place to be. More than 1,200 undergraduate, post-baccalaureate, and graduate students are pursuing licensure programs in elementary and secondary, special education, as well as speech-language pathology and school psychology. In response to a statewide shortage of K-12 educators, speech-language pathologists and school psychologists, Nevada State University has made a strong commitment to building out the SOE to include the following academic programs:  B.A. in Speech Pathology B.A. in Early Childhood and Early Childhood Special Education B.A. in Elementary Education B.A. in Elementary Education with special concentrations in Bilingual and Special Education B.A. in Special Education with a concentration in Autism ​B.A. in Secondary Education with concentrations in English and Social Studies​ ​B.S. in Secondary Education with concentrations in Biology, Mathematics, and Physical Sciences​ M.S. in Speech-Language Pathology Ed.S. in School Psychology​ The School of Education building opened in the summer of 2021; in addition to being home for all SOE programs, faculty, and staff, the facility includes an early childhood education center, a speech-language pathology clinic and a Psychoeducational Mental Health Clinic.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to 4 courses per semester. Teach speech-language pathology courses to graduate and undergraduate students in a variety of formats (e.g., in-person, hybrid, online); majority in person/on campus. Approximately half of this instructional load will be dedicated to core courses in the speech-language curriculum. Undergraduate and/or graduate clinical supervision of clinical practicums either on Nevada State campus or at RiteCare Clinic, as part of course load. Academic advising and mentoring. Collaborate with Nevada State University  colleagues, the local school district, and partner institutions to effectively prepare speech-language pathologists to work in the community.  Participate in service within the School of Education, Nevada State University, and community. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Speech-Language Pathology, Communication and Hearing Sciences or a closely related field.  Candidates who are ABD will be considered with the   expectation that   the Ph.D. or Ed.D. will be completed by December 31, 2026 for a Spring 2027 start date or by June 30, 2027 for a Fall 2027 start date. Current Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP). Eligible for Nevada State Licensure: capability of obtaining Nevada license to practice Speech Language Pathology by start of position.  Demonstrated ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Background in teaching graduate and undergraduate speech pathology courses.  At least three years of clinical experience. Experience with clinical supervision of at least 2 years.   Experience working with diverse, first generation and non-traditional students.  Interested in working with a developing team in an area of expertise. Experience with program oversight and development. Expertise in working with children and/or adult populations. Experience in university teaching and clinical supervision at the graduate level. Experience providing professional development and mentoring SLP instructors. Experience with the ASHA Accreditation Process. Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-Month Tenure Track Budgeted salary for this position: Assistant Professor: $77,164.00 Associate Professor: $91,384.00 Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, November 9, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 8 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted). The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process. Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Intern---School-of-Education-Dean-s-Office-Assistant_R0153385": {
      "title": "Intern - School of Education Dean's Office Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Intern - Dean's Office Assistant for the School of Education. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Event Planning and Coordination Assist with the planning, logistics, and on-site execution of the annual School of Education Summit and the School of Education Gala, including venue setup, vendor coordination, registration, and day-of support. Support additional School of Education events engaging students, faculty, alumni, and community partners, including recruitment events, guest speaker series, and impromptu or short-notice programming. Help develop event timelines, checklists, and post-event summaries to support continuous improvement of future events. Coordinate with campus departments (facilities, catering, marketing, audiovisual services) as needed to support event needs. Social Media and Communications Assist in maintaining and updating the School of Education's social media pages with accurate, timely, and engaging content. Help draft, schedule, and post content that highlights student and faculty achievements, program updates, and upcoming events. Monitor audience engagement and assist in identifying opportunities to grow reach and interaction, in coordination with the Dean's Office and university marketing guidelines. Support the creation of basic graphics, flyers, or promotional materials for events and initiatives. Data Support and Enrollment Analytics Assist administrative staff in compiling, organizing, and updating enrollment and program data using university systems and standard spreadsheet tools. Support the preparation of basic reports, summaries, or visualizations used to inform program planning and decision making. Help maintain accurate records related to enrollment trends and other metrics identified by the Dean's Office. Handle all student and enrollment data in strict accordance with FERPA and university data confidentiality policies. Dean's Office Administrative Support Provide general administrative assistance to the Dean, Associate Dean, and Dean's Office staff, including scheduling, correspondence, filing, and document preparation. Greet and assist visitors, students, faculty, and community guests in a professional and welcoming manner. Assist with routine office operations, including supply management, mail distribution, and maintenance of shared files and calendars. Support special projects and other duties as assigned by Dean's Office staff or the Associate Dean. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Bulleted list of minimum qualifications. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Work Hours: This position will work 15-19.5 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 05/15/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Speech-Language-Pathology-Program_R0153395": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Speech-Language Pathology Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Speech-Language Pathology Program. The student worker will support the Speech-Language Pathology Program located in the Christenson Education Building (CEB). Responsibilities include assisting program faculty, participating in student recruitment events, providing clerical support to the Department Chair for accreditation and program-related needs, and completing other assigned tasks as needed. Some duties may take place at the RiteCare Clinic on Tuesdays or Thursdays. The Department Chair supervises this position. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Working with clinical faculty in preparing client materials, greeting clients in the waiting room, and answering waiting room phones.   Maintaining clinical equipment in working order and organized.  Uploading confidential client paperwork using software.   Working with faculty in course and research support, including but not limited to materials organization, collection and interpretation of data, and reference searches.   Management of materials/equipment checkout system.   Assisting the Department Chair in accreditation and program activities. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher (undergraduate) or 3.0 or higher (graduate). Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits (undergraduate) or 5 credits (graduate) in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).  Strong communication skills in written and spoken English. Knowledge and competency in MSExcel, MSWord.  Attention to detail. Be able to work in an environment of client confidentiality and respect. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Be studying in the field of speech-language pathology, special education, education, health sciences, psychology, biology, or nursing. Bilingual skills—English/Spanish; English/Tagalog. Work Hours: This position will work 10-19.5 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $14.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---STEM-Research-Lab-Technician_R0153391-1": {
      "title": "Student Worker - STEM Research Lab Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - STEM Research Lab Technician . The student worker position supports student and faculty research activities in the department of Physical and Life Sciences (PaLS) by providing hands-on laboratory and technical assistance. This includes supporting students enrolled in independent studies and CURE-based courses, as well as students participating in program-funded and volunteer research, and faculty-led research projects across multiple STEM fields, including microbiology, molecular biology/genetics, chemistry, and physics. The Lab Technician helps maintain laboratory safety, equipment, supplies, and operations and works closely with the Undergraduate Research Program Director and PaLS Department Chair to facilitate research activities and ensure safe and effective laboratory operations. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Research, Technical, and CURE Support Support student and faculty research across multiple STEM fields, including microbiology, molecular biology/genetics, chemistry, and physics. Provide laboratory and technical support for independent studies, program-funded and volunteer research, faculty-led projects, and CURE-based courses. Work closely with the Undergraduate Research Program Director and PaLS Department Chair, following established work instructions and coordinating laboratory support for research and instructional activities. Maintain research organisms, assist with experimental procedures, and prepare reagents, media, and other laboratory materials in accordance with established protocols. Train and assist students in laboratory techniques, equipment use, and safety procedures. Research Documentation and Student Access Verify required safety training and research documentation are completed and in place before students, including volunteers, independent study students, and program-funded researchers, are granted laboratory access or begin research activities. Assist with data collection, recording, processing, and summarization, and maintain accurate research and laboratory records. Laboratory Operations and Maintenance Maintain laboratory equipment, instruments, and facilities, including routine monitoring, calibration, and operational checks. Receive, inventory, organize, and maintain laboratory supplies, chemicals, reagents, glassware, and consumables. Report equipment or laboratory issues and coordinate repairs with appropriate facilities or service units. Manage biological and chemical waste in accordance with institutional and regulatory requirements. Laboratory Safety and Compliance Monitor laboratory activities and maintain a safe, clean, organized, and functional environment in accordance with institutional and regulatory requirements. Ensure students and faculty working in the laboratory have completed required safety training and follow applicable laboratory safety protocols. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.5 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Currently enrolled at Nevada State in a program with coursework in biology, chemistry, biochemistry, or a related field. Research experience in a wet-lab setting, or have completed a summer research programs such as INBRE- iSURF, UROP, EPSCoR, or NASA-funded programs. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: GPA of 3.0 or higher. Successful completion of BIOL 300L and a Molecular Biology course, other upper-division biology or chemistry laboratory courses. Proficiency in molecular biology techniques such as PCR, gel electrophoresis, DNA extraction, and bacterial transformation. Currently entering junior or senior year of undergraduate study. Work Hours: This position will work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $16.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Nursing_R0153227": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University School of Nursing has three 12-month tenure track faculty position available starting January 2027. The Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing position is primarily dedicated to a growing on-the-ground pre-licensure BSN program. This is not a remote position. About the School of Nursing at Nevada State: We are seeking outstanding nurse educators to work alongside dedicated faculty and staff in a highly collegial, interdisciplinary environment based on Caring Science. In the School of Nursing, Caring Science is infused throughout the curriculum and influences how faculty, staff, and students interact to achieve the institutional teaching mission. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach 30 credits per academic year across three semesters. Teach upper-level courses in the Bachelor of Science in Nursing program in a variety of formats (e.g., in-person lab, clinical and/or didactic, hybrid, online). Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Conduct required weekly office hours. Be available to students, staff, and faculty. Student advising. Participate in college-wide events. Engage in scholarly activity in accordance with expectations for promotion and tenure. Use experience as a nurse educator to act as a faculty resource. Other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School of Nursing. Required Qualifications: PhD, doctoral degree in nursing, or doctoral degree in a related discipline from an institution accredited by an organization recognized by the Department of Education. MSN degree from an institution accredited by an organization recognized by the Department of Education. Active and unencumbered RN license in Nevada, or eligible to obtain it by endorsement. At least three (3) years of direct patient care experience. Evidence of strong commitment to teaching, mentoring, and working with undergraduate nursing students. Evidence of teaching excellence in nursing at the college/university level. Proof of creative activities consistent with a tenure-track faculty rank. Evidence of leadership ability, and ability to act as a resource in helping to develop new nurse educators. Commitment to creating an academic environment that supports students while holding them accountable for meeting minimum expectations. Personal commitment to professional accountability and behaviors. Commitment to the promotion of Caring Science in every interaction with faculty, staff, students, and stakeholders. Highly effective oral communication, written communication, and interpersonal skills. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Certified Nurse Educator (CNE). Full-time experience teaching nursing at the BSN, or higher, degree level. Previous experience with higher education nursing curriculum and/or course development. Previous experience with accreditation (CCNE, CNEA, ACEN, or regional academic agencies). Experience with technology enhanced education, both simulation and online. Active participation in professional organizations. Rank, Salary & Benefits: 12-month Tenure track Budgeted salary for this position: Assistant Professor: $98,400.00 Associate Professor: $108,000.00 Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, 24 annual leave days, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Thursday, September 10, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply before September 9 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted). The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process. Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date 12/31/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Intern---School-of-Nursing-Operations-Assistant_R0153366": {
      "title": "Intern - School of Nursing Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Intern - School of Nursing Operations Assistant. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Events: Support the planning and execution of multiple events throughout the year. This will include spreadsheet organization, marketing support including communications and social media. Connected to these events will be program develop. Help develop programs to engage students and alumni in the professional development events we will implement. Flyer creation may be a part of this work as well as survey management.  Alumni and friends Operations: Support the management of the alumni committee and alumni ambassadors. Take notes, organize spreadsheets, documents, files. Attend alumni committee meetings. Support assistant Dean in implementing effective alumni engagement. Support in sending out communications, social media posts, etc. Also checking feedback surveys and website updates  Communications and community relations: Support SON communication efforts to help increase awareness in the community about the school of nursing. This may include website research, community outreach through different forms of communication, document development, etc.   Recruitment and marketing support: Support marketing and recruitment efforts for SON. This will include idea generation, spreadsheet tracking, email communications, word document management. Flyer creation may be a part of this work as well as survey management.   Operational Support: Provide support to various operational needs. This will include data management, spreadsheet tracking, email communication, social media communication, document management, etc. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Bulleted list of minimum qualifications. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Work Hours: This position will work 10 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 05/15/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Intern---Student-Affairs-Marketing-and-Outreach_R0153364": {
      "title": "Intern - Student Affairs Marketing and Outreach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Intern - Student Affairs Marketing & Outreach. The Marketing & Outreach Intern will work directly with the Vice President of Student Affairs to plan, create, and distribute content that promotes departmental programs, events, and student resources. This is a hands-on role for a student who wants real, portfolio-ready experience in marketing, social media strategy, graphic design, and event promotion. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Marketing and Promotional Responsibilities Draft, schedule, and publish content across the division's social media channels (Instagram, Facebook, and others), including graphics, captions, and short-form video. Design flyers, digital signage, email graphics, and event one-pagers using Canva for programs such as welcome week, wellness fairs, and leadership workshops as requested by supervisor Maintain and update the division's webpages and event calendar listings to keep information accurate and current. Photograph and video-capture student events for use in recap content and future promotional materials. Departmental Events Engagement Track basic engagement metrics (reach, clicks, RSVPs) and summarize results in a brief weekly report  Support tabling events and outreach pop-ups by preparing materials and staffing information tables alongside professional staff. Special Projects Special projects: the intern will be assigned at least one ongoing departmental project per semester — past examples include a rebrand of a department's Instagram presence, a student-voice video series, and a print/digital campaign for a division-wide event. The intern will help scope, execute, and present results on this project at the end of the term. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Bulleted list of minimum qualifications. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Work Hours: This position will work 15 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 05/15/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
