    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Intern---School-of-Nursing-Social-Media_R0153324-1": {
      "title": "Intern - School of Nursing Social Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Intern - School of Nursing (SON) Social Media. The student worker the intern will design, implement, and evaluate a social media campaign (primary focus) and assist with event planning/programming (secondary focus) that together enhance SON’s visibility and engagement with internal and external audiences. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Conduct research on best practices from peer institutions. Develop a content calendar and manage postings. Create multimedia content (graphics, reels, infographics, short videos). Monitor engagement and track analytics (reach, impressions, follower growth). Assist in planning SON events (SON open house, application workshops/info sessions, outreach/recruitment, info sessions). Support promotion of events via social media campaigns. Capture event highlights for future content. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 3.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Majoring or minoring in a relevant degree program for the duties/responsibilities assigned for any internship positions applying to. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Strong writing and storytelling abilities. Comfortable conducting both planned and impromptu interviews. Familiarity with social media platforms. Basic graphic design, videography and video editing skills (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite) Interest in higher education marketing Experience with social media analytics reporting. Work Hours: This position will work 12-15 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 05/15/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Dawson-Campus/Student-Worker---Student-Wellness_R0153043": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Student Wellness",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Student Wellness. The Student Wellness Team is committed to fostering holistic student wellness through collaborative, inclusive, and student-centered support. Our mission is to empower students by helping them identify and address challenges, develop essential skills, and gain insights that lead to positive personal growth. Through advocacy and empowerment, we strive to create a nurturing environment that supports the mental, physical, and emotional health of all students, ensuring they have the opportunity to thrive throughout their journey at Nevada State University. This position plays an essential role in supporting food security initiatives across campus. This position assists with maintaining the full-sized pantry, mini-pantry, and wellness snack box locations to ensure students have consistent, dignified access to food resources. The student worker will support inventory management, restocking, organization, and basic front-facing service functions while upholding the values of confidentiality, respect, and care. This role is ideal for a student who is dependable, detail-oriented, and committed to supporting the well-being of fellow Scorpions. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Food Pantry & Snack Box Operations Restock and organize the main food pantry, mini-pantry, and campus snack box locations. Monitor inventory levels and communicate restocking needs. Assist with receiving, sorting, and organizing food deliveries and donations. Ensure pantry spaces are clean, orderly, welcoming, and accessible. Inventory & Data Support Assist with tracking inventory and usage patterns. Support basic data entry related to pantry distribution. Maintain organized storage systems and labeling. Confidentiality & Student Support Greet students accessing pantry resources in a respectful and welcoming manner. Provide basic information about Student Wellness services. Assist students with understanding pantry processes as needed. Maintain confidentiality and exercise diligence with sensitive information. Uphold the office’s commitment to service quality, student empowerment, diversity, and respect. Outreach & Engagement Support Assist with awareness efforts related to food security initiatives. Support tabling events or campus engagement activities as assigned. Support additional Student Wellness initiatives as assigned. Training & Development Participate in initial and ongoing training related to student wellness, food insecurity awareness, and campus resources. Learn and follow all Student Wellness policies and procedures. General Office Support Assist with light administrative tasks. Answer phones, take messages, and route inquiries appropriately. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.5 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Excellent communication and customer service skills. Exhibit leadership and initiative; be dependable, display self-discipline and professionalism. Exercise good judgment and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential matters. Knowledge of computer applications, office systems, and procedures. Ability to follow instructions, show initiative, work well with others, and stay focused. Accuracy and attention to detail. Work effectively as part of a collaborative and diverse team. Respond promptly to changing priorities. Learn new tasks quickly. Ability to lift and carry moderate-weight items (food boxes and supplies) as needed. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Work Hours: This position will work 10-15 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Teacher-Education---Literacy-Education_R0151008": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Teacher Education - Literacy Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of Teacher Education - Literacy Education to start either Spring 2027 or Fall 2027, negotiated upon offer. The Assistant/Associate Professor will contribute to program development and academic leadership. Qualified candidates may be considered for program director or department chair responsibilities. Nevada State University is designated as a Hispanic-Serving Institution and we are looking for candidates with a demonstrated commitment to and success working in diverse, multicultural, and multilingual communities. Our program seeks candidates who are passionate about fostering success among our highly diverse student population as well as preparing educators to advocate in a similar manner for their own students. Candidates should be able to teach literacy methods courses, particularly courses with a focus on emergent literacy development, and content literacy courses with a focus on reading to learn. Candidate should be prepared to teach foundational literacy courses addressing phonics, phonemic awareness, and evidence-based early reading instruction. Candidates should be able to provide examples of integrating a social justice framework into all courses.  About the School of Education at Nevada State: The School of Education (SOE) is an exciting place to be. More than 1,200 undergraduate, post-baccalaureate, and graduate students are pursuing licensure programs in elementary and secondary, special education, as well as speech-language pathology and school psychology. In response to a statewide shortage of K-12 educators, speech-language pathologists and school psychologists, Nevada State has made a strong commitment to building out the SOE to include the following additional academic programs:  Master’s Degree in Speech-Pathology   Baccalaureate Degree in Elementary Education with Emphasis in Bilingual Education   Baccalaureate program in Inclusive Early Childhood Education (EC/ECSE)   Ed.S. in School Psychology  Bachelor of Arts in Special Education with a Concentration in Autism  The new School of Education building opened in the summer of 2021; in addition to being home for all SOE programs, faculty, and staff, the new facility includes an early childhood education center, a speech-language pathology clinic and a Psychoeducational Mental Health Clinic.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teach lower- and upper-level courses in Teacher Education and Literacy in a variety of formats (e.g., in-person, hybrid, online). Approximately half of this instructional load will be dedicated to core courses in the literacy curriculum. Fulfill service obligations to the School of Education, Nevada State University, our local community as well as the discipline-specific professional community. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Literacy, Curriculum and Instruction, Teacher Education or a related field (Candidates who are ABD will be considered with the expectation that the Ph.D. or Ed.D. will be completed by December 31, 2026 for a Spring 2027 start date or by June 30, 2027 for a Fall 2027 start date).  At least three (3) years teaching literacy in a K-5 setting.  Certification or eligibility for certification in Nevada.  Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence, teacher preparation, and student success.  Demonstrated dedication to or interest in working with a diverse student population.  Commitment to teaching literacy/methods courses.  Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching early childhood literacy. Commitment to teach literacy/methods courses. Expertise in curriculum mapping and program development. Experience advising undergraduate pre-service teachers, school-university partnerships, and contributing to program assessment, and accreditation processes. Experience with program mapping and program development. Experience in web-based learning management systems (Nevada State uses Canvas) and multiple course modalities (online, hybrid, in-person). Experience with (or desire to teach) online, hybrid, or evening classes. Research expertise in early, adolescent, or disciplinary literacy. Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure or Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is commensurate with experience. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, September 14, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by September 13 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted). The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process. Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Office-and-Programing-Assistant_R0153247": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Office and Programing Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Office and Programing Assistant for the Center for Teaching and Learning Excellence (CTLE). About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Administrative/Clerical Provide support to the CTLE staff with projects or tasks. Record attendance for CTLE events. Collect and summarize comments from feedback forms. Assist in generating reports. Scanning and copying. Event and Program Management Assist with room reservations. Assist with set-up and clean-up for events. Assist getting students more involved and obtaining feedback and suggestions from students on innovative teaching and learning activities. Participate in CTLE Staff/Team meeting reports. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.5 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise diligence with confidential information and materials. Familiar with the use of Microsoft Word and Outlook. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to work and manage multiple duties and projects to meet established deadlines. Ability to operate standard office machines. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Maintain a GPA of 3.0 or higher. Familiar with the use of Power Point, Excel, Adobe, Canva, etc. Strong understanding of grammatical mechanics to edit copy materials. Work experience in an office setting. Experience working with events/meetings. Work Hours: This position will work 19.5 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Career-Ambassador_R0153200": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Career Ambassador",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Career Ambassador. The student worker will be an integral component in providing career development services to Nevada State students in the Career Services Center (CSC). Career Ambassadors will be required to go through ongoing paid training prior to the start of each semester. We are interested in applicants who are motivated, able to learn new skills quickly, enjoy helping others, and are detail-oriented. Interested applicants should be comfortable with a high level of responsibility and in good academic standing.  Professionalism and a willingness to help others is a must. Career Ambassadors must possess excellent communication (both written and verbal) skills as well as an ability to connect with diverse individuals. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Customer Service & Student Success Support Provide friendly and attentive customer service; greeting and assisting students, alumni and prospective students and their families with general questions regarding CSC services and resources; answer office phone calls and walk-in questions.  Conduct outreach to students enrolled in our Undeclared Exploratory Freshman career advising initiative to encourage students to schedule their required 1:1 appointment with our Freshman/Sophomore Career Advisor.    Conduct outreach to follow-up and collect data on CSC events, services provided, etc. as requested.   Conduct pop-up tabling on campus to inform students of our services and direct them to our office.  Event Planning & Facilitation Assist with the implementation of career development workshops and events (help with set-up, check-in, take-down, etc.), including large-scale events such as career fairs.  As schedule allows, help facilitate presentations to Nevada State classes on the center’s resources and services.  General Administrative Duties Help sort incoming donations to the Career Services Career Closet.  Conduct data analysis and compile reports for programming and initiatives upon request.  Support management of departmental online platforms including posting job and internship opportunities on our Handshake college career networking site  Other Duties as Assigned Students will have the opportunity to propose and /or co-develop new role responsibilities based on their skill set and interests. Each student will be assigned responsibilities that align with both departmental need and student career aspirations.  Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 3.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Ability to maintain a positive attitude, demonstrate excellent customer services skills and foster a welcoming rapport. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Exhibit leadership and initiative; be dependable, display self-discipline and professionalism. Must demonstrate ability to maintain FERPA standards and manage sensitive information. Ability to work independently and on a team. Strong knowledge of Microsoft Office programs with proficiency in Excel, PowerPoint, and Word. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of available student support services at Nevada State. Able to work flexible hours (some evenings/weekends; student workers will always be notified well in advance of any evening or weekend hours; evening/weekend hours are rare but may be required a few times per year). Work Hours: This position will work 12-19.5 hours per week, Monday through Friday, between the hours of 8am-5pm. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Occasionally, Career Ambassadors will be asked to work weeknights and/or weekends to assist with career-related events. Career Ambassadors are required to attend paid training prior to the beginning of each fall semester.  Hourly Rate: $14.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---MARCOS-Scholar-Program_R0153196": {
      "title": "Student Worker - MARCOS Scholar Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - MARCOS Scholar Program. The student worker will provide key social media, student outreach, and advertising support for the MARCOS Program. Additional duties will bolster Student Wellness and access to the Food Pantry. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Manage social media accounts: Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok to help promote scholarship, research, and food accessibility to students. Analyze community-based resources for low-income students. Create fliers to advertise MARCOS and Student Wellness Events. Support new student recruitment initiatives. Assist with MARCOS student outreach, tabling, and support of student wellness initiatives. Increase access to student wellness:  Assist with research to identify community-based referral sources that meet the demographic & support needs of our students (food insecurity, housing insecurity, mental health, financial assistance, legal aid, etc.). Assist with food pantry initiatives & management (inventory support/stocking of food accessibility location). Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 3.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Strong written and verbal communication skills , with the ability to communicate clearly and professionally with students, campus partners, and community organizations. Basic proficiency with social media platforms (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok), including posting content and engaging with audiences. Ability to create simple promotional materials , such as fliers or digital graphics, using Canva, PowerPoint, or similar tools. Interest in student wellness, food access, or community engagement , particularly for underserved or low-income student populations. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Comfort interacting with students in public-facing settings , such as tabling, outreach events, and recruitment activities. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism when handling sensitive student or resource-related information. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to assist with survey coding in Qualtrics. MARCOS supported STEM background (Psychology, Biology, Chemistry, or Environmental Sciences). Comfortable with data analysis and/or creation of Outcome Dashboards for Program Assessment. Work Hours: This position will work 10 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
