    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Business_R0152256": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Business. The student worker will provide support to the Director of the Department of Business and to the Business faculty. Duties include managing various components of the department’s general administrative operations, as well as contributing to special projects. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Administrative support to the Director of the Department of Business and to the Business faculty. Meetings and event coordination. Creating/editing program support materials. Managing social media accounts. Assigned special projects. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Strong organizational skills, an attention to detail, and the ability to multitask. Ability to work with Microsoft Office Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook. Strong writing and information research skills. Please note:  Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Completion of at least 60 credit hours towards degree. Experience creating/editing program support materials. Experience with design software, such as Canva. Experience coordinating meetings and events. Experience creating/managing social media accounts. Work Hours: Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Nursing-Course-Assistant_R0152307": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Nursing Course Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Nursing Course Assistant. The Nursing Course Assistant (Nursing CA) encompasses various support roles for School of Nursing students like Supplemental Instruction (SI) Leaders, Tutors, Peer Mentors, Peer Coaches, and Peer Assistant Lab Specialists (PALS).   In these positions, Nursing CAs provide support in both theory and skills areas through SI sessions, providing one-on-one and group tutoring sessions, nursing skills practice, coaching, and guidance and mentorship. The position may require weekday, weekend, and evening hours as needed.  About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Nursing Course Assistants are trained to provide various supports. They help students engage fully with nursing content and materials and possess the skills to identify and address the academic challenges they may face. Responsibilities may include:  Attending all lectures of the assigned classes, model successful learning behaviors.    Planning, with faculty support, and run weekly supplemental instruction (SI) sessions.    Providing one-on-one and group tutoring. Helping coach students toward success .   Providing nursing skills support.    Notifying students of upcoming workshops and events, as well as methods of support outside their specific scopes.   Meeting regularly with the NSSC staff and provide feedback to facilitate growth of the department. Meeting regularly with collaborating instructor. Providing administrative support as needed.    Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 3.0 or higher.  Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State.  Must be a current pre-licensure BSN student, within the Nevada State University, School of Nursing  Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).  Attends all required trainings every semester that will occur during the two-week period prior to the start of the new semester.    Attends all required meetings or professional training during the week or weekends and school breaks.    Excellent verbal and written communication skills.    Strong work ethic, initiative, ability to work independently.    Ability to work in groups.    Values collaboration.    Outstanding customer service skills.    Maintain confidentiality and exercise extreme diligence with confidential information and materials.    Enjoys talking about the course subject.    Ability to work with faculty, staff and students.    Excellent interpersonal skills with a positive attitude.  Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience teaching, tutoring, or mentoring.    Strong organizational skills.    Knowledgeable of (or able to obtain information about) student-relevant dates and policies such as -but not limited to- add/drop dates, financial aid, academic standing, chain of command, etc.    Knowledgeable of other student support services that Nevada State students can access (training will be provided to supplement existing knowledge of Nevada State resources).  Work Hours: Anticipated number of hours per week is around 8-10 hours, but the actual number of hours may vary up to as many as 19.5 hours during training and special event weeks. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $16.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of class schedule and proof of current GPA; Please provide two (2) faculty references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Name and email address of the course instructor. Should be a Nevada State University instructor who teaches the courses/subject you wish to support or can speak to your strengths for this role. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Registrar-s-Office_R0151926": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Registrar's Office",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Registrar’s Office. The student worker will support students, faculty, and staff with registration and student record services. This position provides hands-on experience in customer service, university operations, and student information systems while helping students navigating processes such as class registration, transcript requests, and their Student Center. Student employees will develop strong communication, problem-solving, critical thinking, and organizational skills while maintaining professionalism, accuracy, and confidentiality in a fast-paced office environment. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Provide friendly and professional customer services to students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors through phone, email, and in-person interactions. Assist students with registration questions and help troubleshoot enrollment issues while applying university policies and Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) guidelines. Help manage, review, and organize student records using university systems such as OnBase and PeopleSoft, including scanning, filing, and data entry. Process Registrar’s Office requests such as, but not limited to, transcripts, enrollment verifications, and student information updates with accuracy and attention to detail. Communicate with students regarding missing documents or next steps needed to complete requests. Maintain confidentiality and responsibly handle sensitive student information. Learn and apply Nevada State University policies and procedures related to registration and student records. Create and give presentations or peer support sessions on topics such as the Student Center and registering for classes. Perform other duties as assigned to promote overall operations and success of the Registrar’s Office. Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Strong verbal and written communication skills. Experience with computer applications such as Microsoft Office. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Customer service experience/ maintain positive attitude in a fast-paced work environment. Ability to work alone and independently, self-directed, detailed-orientated, and able to multitask. Dependable and recognize the importance of being punctual, reliable, and trustworthy. Work Hours: This position will work 19.5 hours per week. Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 48.8% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .  Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Student-Life-Activities-Board-Leader_R0152292": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Student Life Activities Board Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Student Life Activities Board Leader. The student worker will support the Student Life Activities Board which is a student-driven organization dedicated to creating, planning, and executing campus-wide events to encourage a vibrant campus culture at Nevada State. The Student Life Activities Board provides opportunities for students to develop leadership and event-planning skills as well as a way for students to become more connected to the campus community. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities: Help students feel welcomed and connected to the Nevada State University community by planning large-scale and small-scale events and programming through the Office of Student life. Track and manage an annual budget for the Student Life Activities Board. Provide excellent communication and costumer service to any students or vendors inquiring about programs. Meet one-on-one with Student Life Activities Board Advisor for check ins and professional development. Maintain accurate records of receipts, invoices, and any purchase orders made for the year. Provide a monthly report to the Nevada State Student Alliance on expenditures and event attendance. Support in the creation of promotional items and marketing of all student life activities. Help create post-attendance surveys to gather information and data to better provide a campus life experience at Nevada State. Provide input on events effectiveness and suggest improvements based on mentee interactions and outcomes. Work effectively with other Student Life and NSSA student workers, staff, and campus partners to ensure coordinated support for students. Support Nevada State large scale events (Convocation, Commencement and other events). Minimum Qualifications: Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Strong interpersonal, communication, and teamwork skills. Be creative and demonstrate personal initiative. Willingness to create an engaging and robust campus life. Flexible and open schedule availability for events/programs. Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience working on campus. Previous experience in a customer service-driven position. Familiarity with BeEngaged.nevadastate.edu and how to maximize its value as an end-user. Experience using Canva or other platforms for creating promotional items. Work Hours: This position will work 19.5 hours per week. Scheduled hours may be outside of the Monday through Friday, 9am to 5pm office hours due to events/programs. Hourly Rate: $12.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .  Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 | 702-992-2611 | career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Student-Worker---Student-Life-Assistant_R0152291": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Student Life Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Student Worker - Student Life Assistant. The Office of Student Life exists to facilitate student learning and engagement opportunities that build community and promote holistic well-being and transformative development of the Nevada State Student body. The Student Life Assistant position will support this mission by being a key player in the Office of Student Life’s mission to build a culture of involvement by directly serving students by getting them connected to the campus community. This role requires a significant level of autonomy and responsibility.  About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.   We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities:   Serve as a peer coach for the Be Engaged Match Up program, including meeting one-on-one with students and providing personalized recommendations for student organizations and other on-campus involvement opportunities. Work directly with the Coordinator of Student Life to plan and execute large-scale campus events. Independently manage projects as assigned to advance the mission of the Office of Student Life, such as social media, planning workshops, and planning and executing events. Work directly with the Coordinator of Student Life to support the organizational development of student-driven clubs, including developing training materials, planning semesterly club fairs, serving as the co-chair of the Clubs and Orgs Council, and meeting one-on-one with club leaders. Enhance the daily operations of the Student Involvement Hub by doing passive and active programming, identifying and creating resources to improve the space, answering all phone inquiries from the University’s main line, and providing guidance to guests in the Rogers Student Center. Additional Opportunities:    Earn the credential of being a NASPA Certified Peer Educator. Staff the Welcome Desk in the Rogers Student Center Lobby.  Minimum Qualifications:   Must be in good academic standing and maintain a GPA of 2.0 or higher. Must be enrolled as a degree seeking student with a minimum of 6 credits in the current or upcoming semester at Nevada State. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).  Please note:  Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.  Preferred Qualifications:   Experience creating content for social media platforms such as Instagram, TikTok, and Reels. Ability to work independently and take initiative to generate new ideas for the Office of Student Life. Previous experience working on campus. Previous experience in a customer service driven position. Familiarity with BeEngaged.nevadastate.edu and how to maximize its value as an end-user. Experience using Microsoft Office.  Work Hours: Student employees can work up to 19.5 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $14.00 per hour. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 0.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review.  To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at  apply@nevadastate.edu .      Please upload the following documents:  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Copy of Fall or Spring schedule and proof of current GPA; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted).    Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered.     Student candidates are encouraged to visit the Career Services Center (RSC 128 |  702-992-2611  |  career@nevadastate.edu ) to receive assistance with their resume, cover letter, and/or interview skills.   Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant-3---Office-of-Student-Academic-Success_R0152345": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 3 - Office of Student Academic Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Administrative Assistant 3 . The Administrative Assistant 3 will provide high-level administrative, operational, and fiscal support to the Office of Student Academic Success, including the Academic Success Center, Writing Center, and Academic Enrichment Programs & Summer Bridge. This position coordinates office operations, communications, meetings, travel, purchasing, financial processes, events, and special projects while serving as a liaison with internal and external stakeholders and supporting division priorities. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Coordinate and perform administrative and operational support activities for the Office of Student Academic Success and its reporting units, ensuring efficient office operations and alignment with leadership priorities. Manage calendars, meetings, travel arrangements, communications, committees, and special projects; serve as a liaison to faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders by facilitating communication and responding to inquiries regarding programs, services, policies, and procedures. Research issues, resolve problems, and exercise independent judgment in handling sensitive and confidential information. Maintain records, reports, website content, and administrative documentation to support information management and operational effectiveness. Coordinate and perform business and financial operations, including purchasing, procurement card reconciliation, travel processing, budget monitoring, contract administration, and financial recordkeeping. Coordinate events, trainings, and special projects, including facilities scheduling, technology support, vendor communication, marketing coordination, and event logistics. Provide administrative support and operational continuity during staff absences and perform related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Graduation from high school or equivalent education and three years of progressively responsible relevant work experience which included experience in one or more of the following areas: maintenance of complex records and files; public/customer relations including explaining detailed policies, regulations and requirements; preparation and processing of financial and statistical documents such as payroll, travel, claims and budgeting forms; and assisting staff and management with projects and activities; OR one year of experience as an Administrative Assistant 2 in Nevada State service; OR an equivalent combination of education and experience as described above. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing advanced administrative support in a higher education, public sector, or similarly complex environment. Experience coordinating purchasing, travel, budget tracking, contracts, or other business operations. Experience planning meetings, events, or special projects involving multiple stakeholders. Experience interpreting and applying policies, procedures, and administrative guidelines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, Workday, and related administrative systems. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain confidentiality, and work independently. Strong organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Salary & Benefits Budgeted salary for this position is $46,207.44. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including a generous vacation & sick benefits, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, a choice between three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts, and an excellent pension retirement plan through the Public Employees’ Retirement System of Nevada. The plan requires employees to withhold 19.25% of the budgeted salary toward retirement with an equal employer match of 19.25%. No relocation assistance is provided for this position. The typical work schedule is Monday through Friday from 8:00 am to 5:00 pm. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Wednesday, July 8, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by July 7 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Travel Reimbursement Out of Area/State Candidates will not be offered travel reimbursement. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted); Veteran Interview Consideration – (optional) – To receive interview consideration for veterans and veterans with a service-connected disability, proof is required at the time of application. Please attach proof electronically to your application under the Resume/CV section. (Examples of acceptable documents include DD-214, disability letter from Veteran's Administration, etc.). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Senior-Director--North-Las-Vegas-Campus_R0152151": {
      "title": "Senior Director, North Las Vegas Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Senior Director of the North Las Vegas Campus. The Senior Campus Director will report directly to the Provost & Vice President of Academic Affairs and work closely with institutional constituents to provide strategic and operational leadership for our first satellite facility, a purpose-built 30,000-square-foot academic center located in North Las Vegas (NLV). This state-of-the-art campus will open in August 2027 with the goal of increasing educational opportunities and attainment for a vibrant community of current and prospective students who exemplify our institutional mission. This position will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and broad access to higher education while employing a student-centered approach, a collaborative leadership style, and the ability to reliably manage the operations of a growing and multifaceted facility. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities This position will oversee the daily operations of the North Las Vegas site and collaborate with institutional leaders to help us achieve our core goals of promoting student success, fostering enrollment growth, and maintaining financial sustainability. The Senior Director will manage a variety of critical onsite functions, including staff supervision and training, supporting on-campus faculty and staff, and providing student services in collaboration with relevant divisions on the main campus in Henderson.  To ensure that the NLV campus meets student and community needs, this position will engage with key constituents in the region, build partnerships with local schools, employers, and community organizations, and monitor enrollment trends to provide academic divisions with information about student demand and interest. Additionally, the Senior Director will manage the site’s operational budget, work with Campus Infrastructure and Information Technology Services regarding facility operations and maintenance, and act as a liaison to people and divisions at the main campus, facilitating open communication about goals and activities. In executing these and other responsibilities, the Senior Director will follow directives established by university leadership while independently resolving challenges, navigating operational decisions, and pursuing opportunities that improve core outcomes. Specific areas of responsibility include: Daily Operations : Oversee daily operational activities, decisions, and solutions and serving as the primary liaison to the building owner, property management team, and contracted service providers. The Senior Director's office will be located at the NLV campus; the goal is to have supervisory support present on campus during operating hours (either directly or by delegation).   Supervision & Training : Select, train, and supervise a small team of full-time staff and student workers to conduct campus operations and address the needs of students and the community.  Student Services & Support : Work closely with Student Services and academic support divisions to provide virtual support to students at the NLV campus (such as support from admissions, tutoring centers, financial services and cashiering, advising, the registrar’s office, student wellness, and student life). Provide generalist one-stop shop support, either directly or through well-trained staff members. Finance & Budget : Collaborate with the supervising authority at the main Nevada State University campus to develop and manage the operating budget of the NLV campus and provide information to support strategic initiative requests. Community Engagement : Connect with community members and local organizations to promote awareness of the NLV campus and gather feedback about campus services and programs. Support Office of Admissions & Recruitment by providing constituents with information about our programs and services and/or directing them to a recruiter. Intercampus Collaboration : Facilitate open communication with constituents from the main campus to maintain effective collaboration and improve outcomes, including relaying information about student support and programming needs/interests observed at the NLV campus. Strategic Enrollment Support : Fulfill responsibilities and seek opportunities designed to support our strategic enrollment goals, including participating in recruitment activities and monitoring and reporting course enrollment trends each term. Facilities & Maintenance : Coordinate facility maintenance, custodial services, and repair requests, ensuring issues are documented, communicated, and resolved in a timely manner to maintain a safe and welcoming environment. Act as liaison to Campus Infrastructure on the main Nevada State University campus and work with Information & Technology Services to ensure tech questions and on-site issues are addressed. Additional Responsibilities : Fulfill other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution or a Bachelor’s degree with at least three (3) years of progressive leadership experience in higher education or a comparable complex organization.   Demonstrated commitment to student success and adapting to serve the needs of working adults and other non-traditional students. Strong written and oral communication skills. Experience supervising a multi-faceted division, organization, or satellite campus. Demonstrated experience managing a balanced operational budget and making strategic resource allocation decisions. Effective interpersonal skills and demonstrated ability to build partnerships with community organizations, schools, and employers. Ability to work independently and contribute to a collaborative team environment while effectively managing multiple responsibilities and a small team of direct reports. Willingness to travel frequently throughout the North Las Vegas (NLV) region and from NLV to the main Nevada State University campus in Henderson. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting student success initiatives or coordinating student services. Ability to analyze and interpret institutional data to inform operational and enrollment decisions, including course scheduling. Evidence of strong customer service skills and the ability to train team members to deliver exceptional service across a range of responsibilities and apply effective performance management and professional growth strategies as needed. Experience with student recruitment, preferably in higher education. Salary & Benefits Budgeted salary for this position is $118,000 . Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, 24 annual leave days, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Tuesday, June 30, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by June 29 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Upload the following documents: Detailed resume or CV listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and explaining your vision for this role; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include all required documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Senior-Director-of-Development_R0151189": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Senior Director of Development . The Senior Director of Development will provide leadership in the Development and Alumni Office through identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of major and principle gift prospects for the Foundation.  In addition, the Senior Director will lead and manage the Alumni Coordinator position, as well as assist the Vice President of Advancement with all aspects of the department, including strategic planning, campaign preparation and the creation and execution of new ideas/events/programs to raise new funds for the University. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2024, the enrollment surpassed 7,500, with 7,464 undergraduate students and 85 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 41% are Hispanic, 13% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 9% are Black/African American, 22% are White, and 6% are multiracial. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.  We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Primary Responsibilities: Identification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship of donors, with an emphasis on gifts above $25,000. Work on building a donor pipeline through prospect identification activities, including participation at external events, utilize moves management strategy for donor progression and create creative stewardship methods. Lead and manage the Alumni Coordinator position, which oversees all alumni relations efforts. With the Vice President of Advancement, plan and execute annual and strategic plans for the division. Serve as the Advancement liaison to one of the three schools within Nevada State University. Attend internal and external events to represent the Division of Advancement and Nevada State University. Embrace a fast moving team environment and work with colleagues with a spirit of partnership, transparency and fiscal responsibility. Support the Vice President of Advancement and the other members of the division in furthering the mission of Nevada State University. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. A minimum of five (5) years experience in fundraising. Knowledge and experience in donor qualification, cultivation, solicitation and stewardship or other equivalent/transferable knowledge. Documented results with soliciting and closing major gifts. Ability to work strategically and creatively with teams of faculty, staff and volunteers in raising major gifts. Knowledge of alumni relations strategies for success. Ability to work independently, in teams and with other divisions across campus. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Raiser’s Edge software. Management experience. Salary & Benefits Budgeted salary for this position is $86,445. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, 24 annual leave days, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts. This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Tuesday, May 26, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by May 25 for full consideration. Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu . Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    }
